0052: Wildcat Lake (Xe3_LPD display 30.02) backport onto drm-kmod's Linux 6.14 i915 display code, which NMXGPU's
xe build compiles as its display layer. Hand-ported from upstream Linux:
  f8e1c3e07db 632633d095b  display version 30.02 device info (3 pipes, ports A, B, TC1, TC2)
  4dfaae643e5 32620e17644  wildcatlake subplatform of pantherlake, INTEL_WCL_IDS
  9465dd7c400              WCL power wells
  0085d49d301              max cdclk 480 MHz on 30.02
  3d77a3280da a63db39a578  DMC i915/xe3lpd_3002_dmc.bin
  9d10de78a37 8147f7a1c08  C10 PHYs on ports A and B
  8383bdca547              Wa_16023981245 on 30.02
  bd031cd19f5 4051c59e2a6  bandwidth parameters (WCL 22 GB/s, PTL 65 GB/s; 6.14 used MTL's 38)
  7565fd5dcb0              Wa_16025573575 (gmbus bit-bashing)
  cffa413f1c9              max source rate HBR3
  25ea7671bdb              one scaler per pipe
  1b85a9b0468 b42b656db13  no pipe joiner on WCL (+ VBT 261 field)
  d0bf684bd42              Xe3 5-bit DDI clock select everywhere (PTL+ fix)
  0f8d0d764cc              Xe3 CDCLK_CTL: CD2X divider 1, no pipe select field (PTL+ fix)
  299843cd7b9              min plane width on PTL+
  eb4796d8625              audio playback in DC_off (PTL)
plus a NullMoth bring-up default: PSR, FBC and DC5/6 off on 30.02 unless set (-DNMX_WCL_SAFE_DISPLAY=0 drops it).

